From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 18:59:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] dosboot: key the planar boot image on target arch, not
 CPU

The planar emit exists because Amiga display hardware is planar and
chunky->planar C2P on a 7MHz 68000 is prohibitively slow. The condition
tested AROS_TARGET_CPU=m68k, which also catches an m68k with a chunky
framebuffer and no blitter, where the planar emit is simply wrong.

Tests AROS_TARGET_ARCH=amiga instead, which is the property the choice
is actually about.
---
 rom/dosboot/mmakefile.src | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rom/dosboot/mmakefile.src b/rom/dosboot/mmakefile.src
index c5f914fb54..87175b3eef 100644
--- a/rom/dosboot/mmakefile.src
+++ b/rom/dosboot/mmakefile.src
@@ -4,13 +4,13 @@ include $(SRCDIR)/config/aros.cfg
 NOMEDIA_IMAGE := nomedia
 
 # Match the asset format to the target's display hardware:
-#  - m68k / native Amiga has PLANAR display hardware. Emit native planar bitplanes
+#  - native Amiga has PLANAR display hardware. Emit native planar bitplanes
 #    so the image can be drawn with BltBitMap (blitter, planar->planar). The
 #    alternative - per-pixel chunky->planar C2P on a 7MHz 68000 - is prohibitively
 #    slow (~seconds per full-image draw).
-#  - other targets (x86/x64 etc.) have a CHUNKY framebuffer, so keep the chunky
+#  - other targets (including non-Amiga m68k) have a CHUNKY framebuffer, so keep the chunky
 #    emit: WriteChunkyPixels writes chunky->chunky with no planar conversion at all.
-ifeq ($(AROS_TARGET_CPU),m68k)
+ifeq ($(AROS_TARGET_ARCH),amiga)
 NOMEDIA_ILBMTOC_FLAGS := -p
 else
 NOMEDIA_ILBMTOC_FLAGS :=
